比如我喜欢回头看看，我27岁时在想什么？

506
00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:11.660
Where was I?
我当时处于什么状态？

507
00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:12.700
What did I care about?
我在意什么？

508
00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:19.620
About, you know, and you see patterns over time when you review your journals.
你知道，当你回顾日记时，你会看到时间的规律。

509
00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:23.940
I see habits, habits of thinking, habits of behavior.
我看到了习惯，思维习惯，行为习惯。

510
00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:27.580
It's really fascinating, you know, but it's so personal.
这真的很迷人，你知道，但它太私密了。

511
00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.580
I don't, I'm not sure.
我不知道，我不确定。

512
00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:34.540
Like in order to give me the freedom to really write it down, I need to know that Angela's
为了让我有真正写下来的自由，我需要知道安吉拉

513
00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.560
going to burn them if anything happens to me.
如果我出了什么事，她会把它们烧掉。

514
00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.220
I told her I will torch them.
我告诉过她，我会把它们付之一炬。

515
00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:40.160
I hope that day doesn't come.
我希望那一天永远不会到来。

516
00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.540
I mean, that's really, really sweet.
我是说，这真的很贴心。

517
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.920
So I'm glad you guys have that.
所以我很高兴你们有这样的约定。

518
00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.040
You need a BFF who can torch.
你需要一个能帮你烧掉日记的死党。

519
00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:47.620
I know.
我知道。

520
00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.040
The problem is mine are all digital.
问题是我的日记全是电子版的。

521
00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.800
So that's an issue.
所以这是个问题。

522
00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:51.800
Well, I.
嗯，我。

523
00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.520
It exists forever.
它会永远存在。

524
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:53.520
It does.
确实。

525
00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.400
And I, I've started a few years ago.
而且我，我是几年前开始的。

526
00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:59.100
I know I'm like a dinosaur, but that, that notes app on my phone.
我知道我像个老古董，但我手机上的那个笔记应用。

527
00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.240
So I love to write comedy.
我喜欢写喜剧。

528
00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.200
I love to like study people.
我喜欢观察人。

529
00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:05.180
So I have a whole notes on my phone.
所以我手机里有一整套笔记。

530
00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:09.480
Jenna, I don't even know if I've ever shared this with you of just observations of people,
珍娜，我甚至不知道有没有跟你分享过，就是对人的观察，

531
00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.920
situations, things that I might find funny.
各种情况，我觉得可能有趣的事情。

532
00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.960
I have a handwritten notebook of that.
我有一个手写的笔记本记录这些。

533
00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:15.580
You do?
真的吗？

534
00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:15.940
Yeah.
是的。

535
00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:17.500
I wrote one down the other day.
前几天我还记了一条。

536
00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:22.620
I said, um, in case I ever need to play characters, I can look at all these notes.
我说，嗯，万一以后需要演什么角色，我可以看看这些笔记。

537
00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.200
Woman who reapplies her lipstick immediately after finishing a meal.
刚吃完饭就立刻补口红的女人。

538
00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:27.960
That's a person.
那确实是个人物。

539
00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:28.460
It is.
没错。

540
00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.120
That's a thing.
那确实是一种现象。

541
00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:29.900
That's a full character.
那是一个完整的角色。

542
00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:34.320
I have a question for both of you because I, I know what some of this stuff is like.
我有个问题想问你们俩，因为我，我知道其中一些东西是什么样的。

543
00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:39.080
What did you hate doing or like the process of, of making?
你们讨厌做或者讨厌制作过程中的什么环节？

544
00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:44.820
By the end of the run, it was less fun to sit in the background of all the scenes.
到拍摄后期，坐在所有场景的背景里就没那么有趣了。

545
00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:49.320
I think about that a lot when I'm watching because you guys really be doing that.
我看剧的时候经常想到这一点，因为你们真的得那样做。

546
00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:53.040
You guys are in the back of a lot of shots.
你们在很多镜头的背景里。

547
00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:53.320
Yeah.
是的。

548
00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:53.680
Everybody.
每个人都是。

549
00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:57.220
Like all of the, the one-offs, like the talking heads.
就像所有的那些，一次性的，比如采访镜头。

550
00:19:57.220 --> 00:20:01.140
And, and you don't even think when you're watching, honestly, I don't even think about
而且，老实说，你看的时候根本不会想到这些。

551
00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:06.340
it unless like I, I, I religiously watch like the bloopers of all the stuff.
除非像我一样，我可是会虔诚地观看所有花絮的人。

552
00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:08.580
And I, and that's when I noticed, I'm like, oh my God.
然后我注意到了，我就想，天哪。

553
00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:10.300
Leslie David Baker.
莱斯利·大卫·贝克。

554
00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:10.560
Yeah.
是啊。

555
00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:12.320
And Creed are in the back.
还有克里德在后面。

556
00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:12.600
Yeah.
没错。

557
00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.900
In the back of every single one.
每一集都在后面。

558
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:15.360
Yeah.
是啊。

559
00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:16.440
I know.
我知道。

560
00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.400
For nine years.
整整九年。

561
00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:18.140
For nine years.
整整九年。

562
00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:18.640
For nine years.
整整九年。

563
00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:21.320
I sometimes lucked out because I was behind a partition.
我有时运气好，因为我躲在隔板后面。

564
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:24.760
And so I could be like, come on guys, you can't see Angela right in here.
所以我可以表现得像，拜托各位，你们在这儿根本看不见安吉拉。

565
00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.280
Come on.
拜托。

566
00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:27.040
You can barely see me when I stand up.
我站起来时你们都几乎看不见我。

567
00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:32.420
I know for me, the thing that really got old was the fake pregnant belly.
对我来说，最让我受不了的就是那个假孕肚。

568
00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:39.520
Because you had a body suit with the belly and it was itchy and heavy.
因为你得穿一件连体衣，肚子又痒又重。

569
00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.880
And Jenna had it firSt.
而且珍娜先穿的。

570
00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:41.320
Right.
没错。

571
00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.940
And she was really griping about it.
她当时一直在抱怨。

572
00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.180
And I was like, okay, all right.
我当时想，好吧，行吧。

573
00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.180
It can't be that bad.
应该没那么糟吧。

574
00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:45.700
Oh God.
天哪。

575
00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.120
And then I had it.
后来轮到我穿了。

576
00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.440
And I was like, are you kidding me with this thing?
我当时想，你在跟我开玩笑吗？

577
00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:51.180
Like to go pee, forget it.
想去上厕所？想都别想。

578
00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.040
You're mic'd under the-
你的麦克风在……下面

579
00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.180
It was 20 minutes to get out of it.
脱掉它得花二十分钟。

580
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:56.000
Under this pillow thing.
在这个枕头状的东西下面。

581
00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:56.340
Wow.
哇。

582
00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:57.420
So it's not just a belly.
所以那不仅仅是个肚子。

583
00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:59.320
It's like a full piece.
它是一整件衣服。

584
00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:00.420
It's like a-
就像个……

585
00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:01.860
It's like a wetsuit.
就像潜水服一样。

586
00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:04.300
But then a little pocket that a belly goes in.
但有个小口袋用来装肚子。

587
00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.440
So your legs and your arms are in that thing.
所以你的腿和胳膊都在那东西里面。

588
00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:06.900
Yeah.
是啊。

589
00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:08.300
You step into it.
你得钻进去。

590
00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:08.740
Right.
没错。

591
00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.200
And how about this?
还有这个呢？

592
00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.300
We haven't gotten there yet.
我们还没聊到那儿呢。

593
00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:16.580
But when Robert California has this big party, we all go in the swimming pool.
罗伯特·加州举办大派对时，我们都跳进了游泳池。

594
00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:19.820
And they had me swim with that fake belly.
他们让我挺着那个假肚子游泳。

595
00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:20.520
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

596
00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.620
It absorbs water.
它会吸水。

597
00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.720
I was like, oh my God.
我当时想，天哪。

598
00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.180
I'm shocked you didn't sink to the bottom with your tiny self.
我真惊讶你那小身板居然没沉到底下去。

599
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:27.780
I know.
可不是嘛。

600
00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:29.500
I got a good core workout.
我倒是练了一次很棒的核心肌群。

601
00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.480
Do you have a favorite season of The Office?
你最喜欢《办公室》的哪一季？

602
00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:33.240
I do.
我有。

603
00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:33.880
You do?
真的吗？

604
00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:34.420
What is it?
是哪一季？

605
00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:34.700
Okay.
好吧。

606
00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.380
Three, four, and also five.
第三、第四，还有第五季。

607
00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.500
But three and four are like unbelievable.
但第三和第四季简直好得不可思议。

608
00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:42.660
Five is also incredible.
第五季也很棒。

609
00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:43.100
Yeah.
没错。

610
00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:43.700
Incredible.
不可思议。

611
00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:48.080
But three and four, like it's just like Jim and Pam get together around there.
但第三和第四季，吉姆和帕姆差不多就是在那时候在一起的。

612
00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.200
Things are good.
一切都很美好。

613
00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.420
We're like, Michael's not leaving yet.
那时候迈克尔还没走。

614
00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:52.740
We're in a good zone, man.
我们正处于一个很好的阶段，伙计。

615
00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:55.040
There's not conflict as much yet.
还没那么多冲突。

616
00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.920
There's not like the senator yet.
还没有参议员那个角色。

617
00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:59.500
There's not Robert California yet.
还没有罗伯特·加利福尼亚。

618
00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:00.740
There's not Joe.
还没有乔。

619
00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:01.760
There's not Gabe yet.
还没有盖博。

620
00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:03.660
And it still, it stays really good.
而且剧集质量一直保持得很好。

621
00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.940
But those just couple seasons are just like happiness.
但那几季简直就是幸福的代名词。

622
00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:08.840
Can I bring you into a controversy?
我可以带你进入一个争议话题吗？

623
00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:09.740
Yeah, please.
好啊，请说。

624
00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:16.660
Do you think that it was okay that Jim bought his parents' house in Frame Tobey without telling Pam first?
你觉得吉姆在《托比陷害》那一集里没先告诉帕姆就买下他父母的房子，这样做合适吗？

625
00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:17.600
Where do you stand?
你的立场是什么？

626
00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:18.760
Interesting.
有意思。

627
00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:20.300
Romantic or controlling?
是浪漫还是控制欲？

628
00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:21.720
I don't love it.
我不太喜欢这样。

629
00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:28.480
But also, people in their relationships have their own what's okay and what's not.
但话说回来，每个人在感情中都有各自的底线。

630
00:22:28.600 --> 00:22:29.380
That's a great answer.
真是个绝妙的回答。

631
00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:32.440
Even though these are not real characters, they are in the show.
虽然他们不是真实存在的人，但他们是剧中的角色。

632
00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:36.580
And it's not, it's up to, it's up to Pam whether it was okay or not.
而且这事儿，到底合不合适，得由帕姆说了算。

633
00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:37.420
Not me.
不是我。

634
00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:37.820
Exactly.
没错。

635
00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:38.220
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

636
00:22:38.220 --> 00:22:40.180
And I think it made Pam like life.
而且我觉得这让帕姆很喜欢这种生活。

637
00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:41.820
She felt so taken care of.
她感到被照顾得很好。

638
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.020
And also what I liked was that at first you're like, you thought this without telling me?
而且我喜欢的一点是，起初你会觉得：你竟然没告诉我？

639
00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.080
And like, look at all these weird things going on.
看着这些奇怪的事情发生。

640
00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:54.180
And you have this whole concern and everyone that's watching is like, yeah, what the hell is going on?
你会产生各种顾虑，所有观众当时都在想：搞什么鬼？

641
00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:54.540
Yeah.
是啊。

642
00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:59.900
And then it's this like very sweet, touching moment of you being like, I love it.
然后紧接着就是一个非常甜蜜、感人的时刻，她表现出：我喜欢这个。

643
00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:00.680
Like, look at this.
就像是，看看这个。

644
00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.920
Like, I don't even care about any of the anything, but you bought me this, you know?
我甚至不在乎其他任何事，但你为我买了房子，你懂吗？

645
00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:06.000
You bought me a house.
你为我买了一栋房子。

646
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:06.580
It's amazing.
这太棒了。

647
00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:10.280
So it's like, I think you can see it from both sides.
所以我觉得你可以从两方面来看。

648
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:14.500
Like, I wouldn't want someone to do that in my life.
如果是我的生活，我可不希望别人这么做。

649
00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:19.240
But also, it's like, it depends on the situation and the person and your life and the thing, you know?
但同时，这也取决于具体情况、当事人、你的生活方式等等，你懂吧？

650
00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:23.280
And I think also what came before it was Roy, who was so noncommittal.
而且我觉得还要考虑到之前罗伊的表现，他总是优柔寡断。

651
00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:24.940
They were engaged for so long.
他们订婚那么久了。

652
00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:25.420
Roy sucks.
罗伊真是烂透了。

653
00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:26.820
And then you meet, yes.
然后你就遇到了，没错。

654
00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:29.800
And then you meet Jim, who's like all in.
然后你遇到了吉姆，他简直是全心全意投入。

655
00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:30.220
Yeah.
是啊。

656
00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:31.840
And how good that must have felt.
那感觉一定很棒吧。

657
00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:33.420
So yeah.
所以，没错。

658
00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:34.220
Yeah, it's true, actually.
是啊，其实是真的。

659
00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:37.360
And someone who didn't do anything for Pam ever.
而那个人从来没为帕姆做过任何事。

660
00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:41.980
And then it's like, yeah, maybe it's so far the other direction that it could be too far.
然后就变成了，嗯，也许这反向走得太远了，甚至有点过头了。

661
00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:48.240
But it's so nothing like she's ever experienced that it's like really touching to do that, you know?
但这种体验是她从未有过的，所以这样做真的很感人，你懂吗？

662
00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:49.100
Which is sweet.
这很贴心。

663
00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:54.860
It's interesting because when that episode came up, I said, and we've had these conversations before.
这很有趣，因为当那一集出现时，我说过，我们以前也进行过类似的对话。

664
00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:58.320
What do you do when something has been written for your character?
当剧本为你这个角色写了某些情节时，你该怎么办？

665
00:23:58.360 --> 00:23:59.480
Yeah, that you don't agree with.
没错，就是那种你不太认同的情节。

666
00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.100
Yeah, that you're like, how do I get behind this?
对，就是那种你会想，我该怎么去接受它呢？

667
00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:04.740
I don't know how to wrap my head around it.
我不知道该怎么去理解它。

668
00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:09.380
And Greg said something similar, which is that Jenna wouldn't like this, but Pam does.
格雷格说了类似的话，他说珍娜可能不喜欢这样，但帕姆喜欢。

669
00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:17.460
And very similarly, Jenna does not like being tickled, but Pam seemed to respond well to it.
同样地，珍娜不喜欢被挠痒痒，但帕姆似乎对此反应良好。

670
00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:20.920
When Roy tickles her, she would always like come around.
当罗伊挠她痒痒时，她总是会顺从。

671
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:22.120
She liked being tickled.
她喜欢被挠痒痒。

672
00:24:22.240 --> 00:24:33.100
And I was like, but this one's really difficult for me because I have a physical, like visceral response to tickling that just causes sort of rage.
我当时就说，但这对我来说真的很难，因为我对挠痒痒有一种生理上的、本能的反应，会让我产生一种愤怒感。

673
00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:34.140
Oh my God, dude.
天哪，伙计。

674
00:24:34.360 --> 00:24:35.920
My mother is over there.
我妈就在那边。

675
00:24:35.940 --> 00:24:36.200
Is this true?
这是真的吗？

676
00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:39.940
I'm getting a thumbs up from your mom.
你妈妈给我竖大拇指了。

677
00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:44.720
I have to resist with all my might hitting the person who tickled me.
我必须拼尽全力忍住不去打那个挠我痒痒的人。

678
00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:45.900
Thank you.
谢谢你。

679
00:24:46.100 --> 00:24:46.920
I feel seen.
我感觉被理解了。

680
00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:49.800
Tickling is a serious thing.
挠痒痒可是件严肃的事。

681
00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:50.980
My brother tickled me.
我哥哥以前也挠我痒痒。

682
00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:55.420
We were in anthropology when I was a little kid and my brother started tickling me.
我小时候我们在人类学博物馆，我哥哥就开始挠我痒痒。

683
00:24:55.520 --> 00:24:58.320
And I had an overreaction to make him feel bad.
为了让他感到愧疚，我反应过度了。

684
00:24:58.440 --> 00:24:59.260
I was like, oh my God, stop.
我当时大喊，天哪，住手。

685
00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:06.680
And I like swung my whole body and I, I bonked myself on the corner of a table and gave myself a black eye.
然后我全身猛地一甩，结果撞到了桌角，把自己撞出了一个黑眼圈。

686
00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:07.280
Oh no.
天哪，不会吧。

687
00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:10.280
And I always blamed him because he was tickling me.
而且我总是怪他，因为是他挠我痒痒的。

688
00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:11.520
Did he ever tickle you again?
他后来还挠过你吗？

689
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:12.180
Yeah.
挠过。

690
00:25:12.540 --> 00:25:12.740
Okay.
好吧。

691
00:25:13.100 --> 00:25:15.540
He did, but, but he, he was scared too.
他挠过，但他也很害怕。

692
00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:17.980
Cause I'd be like, I'll give myself a black eye and I'll blame it on you.
因为我会说，我会把自己撞出黑眼圈，然后全怪在你头上。

693
00:25:18.060 --> 00:25:18.260
Yeah.
没错。

694
00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:20.100
Older brother gets the punishment.
哥哥总是背锅的那个人。

695
00:25:20.100 --> 00:25:25.760
But no, I agree that I'd be furious if somebody bought a house and didn't, didn't ask me or tell me.
不过说真的，我同意如果有人买房而不问我或告诉我，我也会气疯的。

696
00:25:25.920 --> 00:25:26.080
Yeah.
是啊。

697
00:25:26.280 --> 00:25:26.760
Be furious.
会气疯的。

698
00:25:27.160 --> 00:25:28.040
Jenna wouldn't like that.
珍娜肯定不喜欢那样。

699
00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:28.440
Yeah.
没错。

700
00:25:28.600 --> 00:25:31.700
But then it's also like funny when you sell the house.
但当你卖掉房子时，那也挺好笑的。

701
00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:35.100
I'm telling him absolutely bonkers.
我跟他说这简直太疯狂了。

702
00:25:35.320 --> 00:25:35.640
I know.
我知道。

703
00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:36.120
That happens.
这种事常有。

704
00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:37.620
But then it's like, you have a point.
但后来又觉得，你说的也有道理。

705
00:25:37.700 --> 00:25:39.220
You're like, well, you bought it without telling me.
你会想，好吧，你买的时候也没告诉我。

706
00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:40.780
So I thought I could sell it without telling you.
所以我以为我卖的时候也可以不告诉你。

707
00:25:40.980 --> 00:25:44.020
Every time I hear that line, I'm like, unbelievable.
每次听到这句台词，我都觉得，简直不可思议。

708
00:25:44.320 --> 00:25:44.680
I know.
我知道。

709
00:25:44.840 --> 00:25:45.760
Unbelievable statement.
真是不可理喻的说法。

710
00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:47.880
You bought the house without telling me.
你买房子没告诉我。

711
00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:49.360
So I'm like, sell it without telling you.
所以我卖房子也可以不告诉你。

712
00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:50.640
I know it's a weird book.
我知道那本书很奇怪。

713
00:25:50.640 --> 00:25:51.820
It's a crazy relationship.
那段关系很疯狂。

714
00:25:52.040 --> 00:25:54.120
Maybe she had been holding onto it a little bit.
也许她一直对此耿耿于怀。

715
00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:54.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

716
00:25:55.180 --> 00:25:55.600
Clearly.
显然是这样。

717
00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:55.880
Yeah.
是啊。

718
00:25:56.080 --> 00:25:56.300
Clearly.
显然。

719
00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:02.500
I mean, every week I had to like reconcile with a character that was very different from me.
我是说，每周我都得去和那个与我截然不同的角色达成和解。

720
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:03.820
Like, oh yeah.
就像，噢，没错。

721
00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:05.700
All of my reactions, everything.
我所有的反应，所有的一切。

722
00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:08.440
So I, I can really relate to that.
所以我真的能感同身受。

723
00:26:08.580 --> 00:26:13.440
I mean, there were plenty of times where I was like, okay, can we dial Angela back just a little?
我是说，有很多次我都想说，好吧，我们能不能让安吉拉稍微收敛一点？

724
00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:16.160
Like, can she not always just be the bitch?
比如，她能不能别总是那么刻薄？

725
00:26:16.160 --> 00:26:19.400
And I loved that note that Ken Coapis gave me.
我很喜欢肯·科皮斯给我的那个建议。

726
00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:22.900
He was like, Angela, today why don't you try being the suspicious bitch?
他说，安吉拉，今天你为什么不试着演一个多疑的刻薄鬼呢？

727
00:26:23.100 --> 00:26:29.860
And I was like, ooh, she's totally different than like the strict bitch, suspicious bitch.
我就想，噢，这和那种严厉的刻薄鬼、多疑的刻薄鬼完全不同。

728
00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:35.800
Was there anything in Angela's character that you did like resonate with at all?
安吉拉这个角色身上有什么让你产生共鸣的地方吗？

729
00:26:36.100 --> 00:26:37.760
I mean, I do love animals.
我是说，我确实很爱动物。

730
00:26:38.200 --> 00:26:39.360
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

731
00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:40.880
I haven't ever licked my cat.
我从来没舔过我的猫。

732
00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:43.340
I did really do that, Billy.
我真的那样做了，比利。

733
00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:44.620
Yeah, I was going to ask.
是啊，我正想问呢。

734
00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:45.680
I really licked it.
我真的舔了它。

735
00:26:45.740 --> 00:26:46.760
I love that you did.
我喜欢你这么做。

736
00:26:47.140 --> 00:26:48.760
I mean, they were like, it's just one take.
我是说，他们当时说，就拍一条。

737
00:26:48.920 --> 00:26:49.700
We're just one take.
我们只拍一条。

738
00:26:49.780 --> 00:26:50.700
We're going to be a little bit closer.
我们要靠得近一点。

739
00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:54.100
And I was like, oh, and then I licked the cat.
然后我就想，噢，接着我就舔了那只猫。

740
00:26:55.460 --> 00:26:57.340
But I also like Angela.
但我其实也挺喜欢安吉拉的。

741
00:26:59.140 --> 00:27:01.620
She's, once she's in, she's very loyal.
她一旦投入，就非常忠诚。

742
00:27:02.040 --> 00:27:09.420
Like, you know, like I don't think she ever gave up on Dwight, even though they were such a weird on and off again romance.
就像，你知道，我觉得她从未放弃过德怀特，尽管他们的恋情分分合合，非常奇怪。

743
00:27:09.420 --> 00:27:13.240
But he was her soup snake, you know?
但他可是她的“灵魂伴侣”，你知道吧？

744
00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:13.820
It's true.
确实。

745
00:27:14.120 --> 00:27:17.380
So I guess those two things, but pretty much nothing else.
所以我猜大概就是这两点，除此之外几乎没什么共同点。

746
00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:21.080
If you were an office character, which one would you be?
如果你是《办公室》里的一个角色，你会是哪一个？

747
00:27:21.220 --> 00:27:21.620
Good one.
好问题。

748
00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:25.740
I've always really resonated with Michael's character.
我一直都很能和迈克尔这个角色产生共鸣。

749
00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:26.320
Okay.
好吧。

750
00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:28.460
Which is maybe problematic.
这可能有点问题。

751
00:27:28.460 --> 00:27:37.160
I just, and I've said that before to like my mom or like my parents and my brother and stuff.
我只是，而且我以前也跟我妈，或者说跟我父母、我兄弟他们说过。

752
00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:38.860
But it's really true.
但这是真的。

753
00:27:38.980 --> 00:27:47.200
I see a lot of my character and not some stuff like more of just like, I can't even really explain it.
我从他身上看到了很多我自己的影子，不是那种具体的特质，而是……我甚至没法解释。

754
00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:52.180
There's just something that I really, really, really relate to about his character.
他的角色身上确实有些东西让我非常有共鸣。

755
00:27:52.180 --> 00:27:58.640
One of my favorite, favorite moments is when he can't help but shout.
我最最喜欢的时刻之一，就是他忍不住大喊的时候。

756
00:27:58.820 --> 00:27:59.500
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

757
00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:01.860
Even if he's like furious.
哪怕他当时正火冒三丈。

758
00:28:01.860 --> 00:28:07.840
Like when she, when she is about to throw the dundee at the TV and they're having that argument.
比如她快要把邓迪奖杯扔向电视机，两人正在争吵的时候。

759
00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:08.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

760
00:28:08.420 --> 00:28:13.160
And he's like so angry and he's clearly just so sad and like, you know.
他当时那么生气，但显然又那么难过，你知道的。

761
00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:13.540
Yeah.
是啊。

762
00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:16.980
And then she's like, you're hardly my firSt.
然后她说：你才不是我的第一个。

763
00:28:17.040 --> 00:28:22.940
And he's so angry, but he has this need to say that's what she said because he knows I need to say it.
他气得要命，但还是忍不住非要说那句“那是她说的”，因为他知道自己必须得说。

764
00:28:23.020 --> 00:28:24.100
And he just shouts it at her.
于是他对着她大喊了出来。

765
00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:26.420
Michael also just has such a pure heart.
迈克尔其实也有一颗纯洁的心。

766
00:28:26.560 --> 00:28:27.520
He really does.
他确实有。

767
00:28:27.980 --> 00:28:28.180
Yes.
没错。

768
00:28:28.280 --> 00:28:36.400
It's, he's pretty like just a person who just wants love and to be loved, but he goes about it so wonky.
他其实就是一个渴望爱与被爱的人，只是他追求的方式太笨拙了。

769
00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:37.620
But I'm with you.
我赞同你。

770
00:28:37.700 --> 00:28:41.720
Whenever he has to yell something, every time I lose it.
每当他不得不大喊什么的时候，我每次都笑得不行。

771
00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:42.860
Oh, it's so funny.
哦，太搞笑了。

772
00:28:42.860 --> 00:28:46.980
I hadn't seen him yell, I declare bankruptcy until we rewatched it.
重温之前，我都没看过他大喊“我宣布破产”的那一段。

773
00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:47.320
Yeah.
是啊。

774
00:28:47.560 --> 00:28:52.280
And just like his need to do that, to make this announcement is like amazing.
他那种非要这么做、非要搞个大声明的冲动，简直绝了。

775
00:28:52.580 --> 00:28:56.160
It just hurts my soul how he's like, that's how he thinks you declare bankruptcy.
他觉得这就是宣布破产的方式，这让我心里五味杂陈。

776
00:28:56.360 --> 00:28:56.620
I know.
我懂。

777
00:28:56.960 --> 00:28:58.220
You declare it out loud in a room.
你只要在房间里大声喊出来就行了。

778
00:28:58.360 --> 00:28:58.900
It's done.
这就完成了。

779
00:28:59.640 --> 00:29:00.480
I've done it.
我已经宣布过了。

780
00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:01.360
I just feel that.
我太有同感了。

781
00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:01.780
Okay.
好吧。

782
00:29:01.840 --> 00:29:03.580
And this is a part that, that I find.
还有一点，我发现。

783
00:29:03.940 --> 00:29:09.900
So starting, starting to watch The Office at a really young age, I almost didn't understand any reference whatsoever.
因为我很小的时候就开始看《办公室》，几乎完全听不懂里面的任何梗。

784
00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:14.140
I just thought it was funny and I thought, you know, it was, it was funny.
我当时只觉得它很有趣，你知道，就是觉得好笑。

785
00:29:14.140 --> 00:29:18.500
I just liked the show in general, but a lot, most of the references, I had no idea who
我只是单纯喜欢这部剧，但大部分梗我根本不知道

786
00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:21.540
anybody was, no idea what movies they were referencing.
里面指的是谁，也不知道他们引用的是什么电影。

787
00:29:22.460 --> 00:29:28.240
So something I do blame The Office for, to be honest, is, but then also I blame myself,
所以老实说，我确实怪《办公室》，当然我也怪我自己，

788
00:29:28.240 --> 00:29:35.700
but I blame The Office, is, is, there's so many things that are said, especially by Michael
但我怪《办公室》是因为，里面有太多话，尤其是迈克尔说的，

789
00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:41.120
in The Office, that he says wrong on purpose, like written on purpose.
他是故意说错的，剧本里就是这么写的。

790
00:29:41.240 --> 00:29:41.440
Yeah.
没错。

791
00:29:42.220 --> 00:29:44.020
That I didn't even know the real word.
以至于我连正确的词是什么都不知道。

792
00:29:44.020 --> 00:29:48.760
So I said many words wrong because I learned them from Michael Scott.
所以我说错了很多词，因为我是跟迈克尔·斯科特学的。

793
00:29:48.940 --> 00:29:50.020
Were you a little stitious?
你当时是不是有点迷信（little stitious）？

794
00:29:50.340 --> 00:29:52.220
I was a little, that one I knew.
我确实有点，那个词我知道。

795
00:29:54.800 --> 00:30:00.100
That was one that I knew and I was very proud that I knew that one, but like insurmountable,
那个词我知道，而且我很自豪自己知道那个，但像“不可逾越的”（insurmountable）这种词，

796
00:30:00.360 --> 00:30:00.860
to be honeSt.
老实说。

797
00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:02.420
I thought that was a word.
我当时还以为那是个词呢。

798
00:30:02.760 --> 00:30:06.140
I thought, oh no, this has happened many times.
我心想，哦不，这种情况发生过很多次了。

799
00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:12.220
I never thought about this filter of The Office that on a younger person, they're learning
我从没想过《办公室》这层滤镜对年轻人来说，意味着他们正在学习

800
00:30:12.220 --> 00:30:13.460
Michael's vocabulary.
迈克尔的词汇量。

801
00:30:13.700 --> 00:30:14.000
Yes.
是的。

802
00:30:14.280 --> 00:30:15.200
Learning his vocabulary.
学习他的词汇量。

803
00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:17.220
Because I thought I was learning new words.
因为我以为我在学习新单词。

804
00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:17.980
Oh my God.
天哪。

805
00:30:17.980 --> 00:30:18.720
Which I was.
我确实是在学。

806
00:30:18.920 --> 00:30:20.140
They were just wrong.
只是那些词都用错了。

807
00:30:20.400 --> 00:30:24.200
And then, and same when, you know, the joke when Aaron is like, my New Year's resolution
还有，就像那个笑话，你知道的，亚伦说他的新年愿望

808
00:30:24.200 --> 00:30:26.080
was to learn a new word every day.
是每天学一个新单词。

809
00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:26.400
Yeah.
是啊。

810
00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:28.200
And it is going immensely.
而且进展得非常顺利。

811
00:30:28.580 --> 00:30:28.820
Yeah.
是啊。

812
00:30:29.420 --> 00:30:30.360
I didn't get that.
我没听懂那个梗。

813
00:30:30.420 --> 00:30:32.500
I was like, oh cool, I'll start saying that.
我当时想，哦酷，我也要开始这么说。

814
00:30:33.040 --> 00:30:36.120
So now, because I have said so many things wrong.
所以现在，因为我说了太多错话。

815
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:41.560
Mom, do you remember off the top of your head some more ones that I just said that everyone
妈，你还能随口想起我以前说过哪些话，让大家

816
00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:42.820
was like, what the hell?
都一脸困惑吗？

817
00:30:43.280 --> 00:30:46.460
I remember when you first heard that U2 was from Ireland.
我记得你第一次听说U2乐队来自爱尔兰的时候。

818
00:30:46.460 --> 00:30:50.160
Oh, you guys, you guys, you guys, you guys, you guys, you guys, you guys, you guys.
哦，你们，你们，你们，你们，你们，你们，你们，你们。

819
00:30:50.340 --> 00:30:50.680
What?
怎么了？

820
00:30:51.180 --> 00:30:51.620
Okay.
好吧。

821
00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:53.600
This is, this is the worst one.
这个，这个是最糟糕的一个。

822
00:30:54.780 --> 00:30:58.780
Sweet, sweet Bono is, is a supporter of mine.
亲爱的，亲爱的博诺是我的支持者。

823
00:30:58.920 --> 00:30:59.100
Yeah.
是啊。

824
00:30:59.320 --> 00:30:59.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

